            <ArticleTitle>Correctly identifying responses is critical for understanding homeostatic and allostatic regulation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>157-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4161/23328940.2014.982048</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Homeostasis stabilizes critical biological variables within appropriate limits via corrective regulatory effector responses that adequately counter disturbing effects. Identifying individual effects and responses, and distinguishing their individual influences on a regulated state, is challenging. Studying effector responses can reveal regulatory phenomena that depart from homeostasis into the realm of allostasis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
